
Assist me with this Mid-Level Back End Engineer Test
Objective
Design and implement a scalable and maintainable GraphQL API with nestjs that supports a travel planning application. Your consumers should be able to request the following information:
1. Dynamic city suggestions based on partial or complete user input
2. Weather forecasts for a selected city.
3. A ranking of activities based on the weather forecast
a. Skiing
b. Surfing
c. Indoor sightseeing
d. Outdoor Sightseeing
Use the [API](https://open-meteo.com/) for weather and geolocation data.

Focus on clean architecture, thoughtful schema design, and clear documentation.
No frontend implementation is required.

What We’re Evaluating
GraphQL schema design: Clarity, extensibility, and how well it models the domain.
Code quality: Structure, maintainability, and best practices.
Architecture: Separation of concerns, scalability, and testability.
Testing: Presence of meaningful unit and/or integration tests, thoughtful test coverage, and
use of appropriate tools (e.g., Jest, Supertest).
Use of AI tools: How you used AI (e.g., ChatGPT or Copilot) to assist you, and your judgment
in applying the output.
Expected Deliverables
In a GitHub repository:
Codebase: Node.js backend with a GraphQL API.
Open-Meteo
README:
Overview of your architecture and technical choices.
Omissions & trade-offs: What you skipped and why.
How you would improve or extend the project with more time.
Tips for Success
Quality > quantity: It's better to complete one well-designed feature than four rushed ones.
Focus on good abstractions and clean separation between data and logic

